INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'anthropic-residency-ai-safety-20261104', 'global', 'USA',
'Anthropic Residency 2026: $350,000-$500,000 AI Safety Research Programme, Apply by 22 November',
'',
'Anthropic has opened the Anthropic Residency for established technical leaders, paying $350,000 to $500,000 a year pro-rated, with applications closing on 22 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>Anthropic opened applications on 2 November 2026 for the Anthropic Residency, a paid, fixed-term research programme for established technical leaders who want to move into full-time work on AI safety. The company said applications for this round close on 22 November 2026, and the programme offers placements of six weeks, three months, or six months, paid at $350,000 to $500,000 a year on a pro-rated basis.</p>
<p>Read the eligibility bar before anything else, because this is not an entry-level scheme and not a general graduate intake. Anthropic said it wants people who have already led ambitious work in a technical field: professors in quantitative disciplines, technical founders, or staff-level engineers. A background in machine learning is not required, and the company said applicants do not need a PhD, prior machine learning experience, or published papers. The United States posting lists a minimum of a bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education, training, or experience, and says the years of experience required will match the internal level of the role.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Programme</td><td>Anthropic Residency</td></tr><tr><td>Organiser</td><td>Anthropic</td></tr><tr><td>Placements</td><td>Six weeks, three months, or six months; other lengths between three and six months possible by exception</td></tr><tr><td>Pay</td><td>$350,000 to $500,000 a year equivalent, pro-rated for the placement, plus benefits</td></tr><tr><td>Application deadline</td><td>22 November 2026, 11:59 PM Pacific Time</td></tr><tr><td>Offers expected</td><td>January 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>San Francisco preferred; remote participation possible, especially for shorter placements</td></tr><tr><td>Visa sponsorship</td><td>Sponsored for placements of three months or longer; six-week placements are encouraged to be remote from a country where Anthropic can hire</td></tr><tr><td>How to apply</td><td>Through the United States or United Kingdom posting linked from the official announcement</td></tr></table>
<h2>Who the Anthropic Residency is for</h2>
<p>Anthropic framed the round as a way into AI safety for senior people from neighbouring fields. The company said many of its senior researchers started out as physicists, mathematicians, neuroscientists, or software engineers, and that framing a research agenda and judging what is worth doing matter more as model capabilities improve. The Residency is built for people who already show those strengths in another technical field and need structured time, mentorship, and compute to apply them to frontier AI.</p>
<p>The announcement lists the qualities it is looking for in plain terms: a record of leading ambitious technical work, motivation to make AI safe and beneficial for society, enthusiasm for moving into empirical AI research full time, comfort in fast-paced collaborative work, and the ability to put ideas into practice quickly and explain them clearly. The United States posting lists research papers and large language model experience as strengths, not fixed requirements, and the company said applicants should not rule themselves out for missing every single qualification.</p>
<h2>What residents will work on</h2>
<p>Residents work on problems set out by Anthropic researchers and matched to their interests and background, with a concrete, scoped project and direct mentorship. Each resident is paired with an Anthropic mentor and receives regular one-on-one guidance, dedicated self-study time, talks, and support to get up to speed on modern machine learning and AI safety research. Residents also receive a dedicated compute budget and access to frontier models.</p>
<p>The research areas named in the announcement fall into three groups. The first is AI safety and alignment, covering scalable oversight, adversarial robustness and AI control, model organisms of misalignment, model internals and interpretability, safeguards research, and AI welfare. The second is AI security and frontier red-teaming, meaning stress-testing frontier models to map their capabilities in fields such as cybersecurity, robotics, and cryptography. The third is machine learning systems and reinforcement learning, including model architecture, optimisers, training data, accelerator simulators, hardware backends, and reinforcement learning environment pipelines. Mentors named for the round lead teams in alignment training, alignment science, stress-testing, scalable oversight, interpretability, model psychology, adversarial machine learning, and safety and pretraining.</p>
<h2>Pay, place and visas for the Anthropic Residency</h2>
<p>Pay is set at $350,000 to $500,000 a year equivalent, pro-rated for the length of the placement, plus benefits. A three-month placement therefore works out at roughly one quarter of the annual figure before tax. The programme is full time for the duration of the placement, but that is an aim, not a promise of a permanent post.</p>
<p>Place and visas need a careful read for applicants outside the United States. Anthropic said it prefers residents to work from its San Francisco offices, where most of its research staff are based, but remote participation is possible, especially for shorter placements. Remote participants need to be based in a country where Anthropic can hire. Visa sponsorship is offered for placements of three months or longer, while six-week placements are encouraged to be remote from a country where Anthropic can hire. The announcement does not state how many residents this round will take, so applicants should not assume a fixed intake number.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the Anthropic Residency</h2>
<p>Applications go through the United States or United Kingdom posting linked from the official announcement, and applicants should use the posting that matches their location. The United States posting sets out the interview process as an initial application, a recruiter screen, a technical assessment, a research discussion, and a reference check. Applications close on 22 November 2026 at 11:59 PM Pacific Time, and the company said it expects to make offers in January 2027.</p>
<p>Applicants should apply only through the official announcement or the linked postings, and should treat any other route with care. Anthropic said its recruiters only contact applicants from anthropic.com email addresses, and that legitimate recruiters will never ask for money, fees, or banking information before the first day of work. Any message asking for payment to secure a Residency place should be treated as a fraud attempt.</p>
<h2>What to check before applying</h2>
<p>Three points deserve a direct check before an applicant commits. First, the programme is fixed term, so applicants who need a permanent role should weigh that against the senior pay and the research access on offer. Second, the San Francisco preference matters: applicants who cannot relocate should confirm whether their preferred placement length can genuinely be done remotely from their country. Third, no start date is stated beyond flexible timing, so applicants with notice commitments should raise timing at the recruiter screen.</p>
<p>For readers tracking paid routes into AI work, <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-startup-jobs-13514-roles-20261104">AI startup jobs across 1,100 companies</a> cover permanent roles at a median base of $190,000 a year, while <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/ai-training-jobs-consultants-20261104">AI training jobs for consultants</a> pay by the hour. Readers may also want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/periscope-labs-senior-applied-ai-engineer-dhaka-20261104">Periscope Labs Senior Applied AI Engineer post in Dhaka</a>.</p>
<p><small>Sources: Anthropic Alignment Science Blog, "Anthropic Residency: applications open for established technical leaders", published 2 November 2026, at https://alignment.anthropic.com/2026/anthropic-residency/; Anthropic United States posting, "Anthropic Research Resident", at https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5438311008. The announcement states the programme, pay range, placement lengths, deadline, and location preference quoted here; the number of residents this round will take is not stated.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://alignment.anthropic.com/2026/anthropic-residency/','https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/anthropic/jobs/5438311008'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'nicl-graduate-apprentice-200-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'NICL Apprentice Recruitment 2026: 200 Graduate Apprentice Seats, Apply by 18 November',
'',
'National Insurance Company Limited has opened 200 Graduate Apprentice seats across 14 states, with online applications from 4 November 2026 to 18 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>NICL apprentice recruitment 2026 opened on 4 November 2026, with National Insurance Company Limited offering 200 Graduate Apprentice seats across 14 states under the National Apprenticeship Training Scheme for 2026-27. The company said online applications run from 4 November 2026 to 18 November 2026 through the NATS portal, and selected apprentices will receive a monthly stipend of Rs. 15,000 during a 12-month training period.</p>
<p>Read the exclusions before anything else, because they remove a large group of graduates from this drive. The notification excludes candidates who hold a postgraduate degree or have completed an integrated postgraduate course, candidates who have previously undergone apprenticeship training or are undergoing it, candidates whose earlier apprenticeship was terminated midway, and candidates with one year or more of work experience in a government, public-sector, or private organisation as on 1 April 2026. Only regular, full-time graduation in any discipline counts, distance-learning and part-time degrees are not covered by the notification, and each candidate may apply for only one state.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>National Insurance Company Limited (NICL)</td></tr><tr><td>Scheme</td><td>National Apprenticeship Training Scheme (NATS), 2026-27</td></tr><tr><td>Post</td><td>Graduate Apprentice</td></tr><tr><td>Total seats</td><td>200 (provisional)</td></tr><tr><td>States covered</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>Notification date</td><td>4 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>4 November 2026 to 18 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly stipend</td><td>Rs. 15,000 (Rs. 8,850 from NICL plus Rs. 6,150 from the government through direct benefit transfer)</td></tr><tr><td>Training duration</td><td>12 months</td></tr><tr><td>Qualification</td><td>Regular, full-time graduation in any discipline, degree certificate held by 1 April 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>21 to 30 years as on 1 April 2026, with relaxation for eligible reserved categories</td></tr><tr><td>Selection</td><td>Graduation marks-based shortlisting, then physical document verification; no written examination or interview prescribed</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Not specified in the notification</td></tr><tr><td>NATS establishment ID</td><td>EWBPNC096867</td></tr><tr><td>Apply via</td><td>NATS portal, nats.education.gov.in</td></tr></table>
<h2>NICL apprentice recruitment 2026: state-wise seats</h2>
<p>Assam carries the largest allocation, with 30 seats, followed by Gujarat with 22 seats. Chhattisgarh and Rajasthan have 20 seats each, Uttar Pradesh has 14, and Madhya Pradesh and Punjab have 12 each. Jharkhand, Karnataka, Kerala, Maharashtra, Uttarakhand, West Bengal, and Tamil Nadu have 10 seats each. Those figures add up to the advertised total of 200, and the notification says the total is provisional and may increase or decrease according to the company's requirements.</p>
<p>The one-state rule shapes how applicants should choose. Candidates apply for engagement in one state only, and the company reserves the right to allot a selected candidate to any district within the chosen state based on administrative requirements. Applicants should therefore pick a state where they can attend verification in person and complete 12 months of training.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the NICL Graduate Apprentice seats</h2>
<p>Applicants must have completed a regular, full-time graduation degree in any discipline from a university or institution recognised by AICTE, DOTE, or UGC, and must have passed the qualifying examination and held the degree certificate by 1 April 2026. Applicants must also hold a 100 percent complete NATS profile. Applications without the graduation percentage entered in the prescribed NATS profile field will not be considered.</p>
<p>The age limit is 21 to 30 years as on 1 April 2026, with upper-age relaxation for eligible reserved categories: 5 years for Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe candidates, 3 years for Other Backward Classes (non-creamy layer), and 10, 13, and 15 years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities in the general and Economically Weaker Section, Other Backward Classes, and Scheduled Caste and Scheduled Tribe categories respectively. The notified date-of-birth range for general and Economically Weaker Section candidates runs from 1 April 1996 to 1 April 2005, both dates inclusive, subject to the notification's conditions and valid supporting certificates.</p>
<h2>Stipend, training terms, and what this is not</h2>
<p>Selected apprentices will receive a fixed monthly stipend of Rs. 15,000 during the 12-month apprenticeship period, made up of Rs. 8,850 from NICL and Rs. 6,150 from the government through direct benefit transfer into the apprentice's bank account. The notification says the stipend is not a permanent employee salary, and apprentices are not entitled to other NICL employee allowances or benefits. Apprentices earn one day of leave per month of training, subject to prior approval, with a maximum of four days at one time.</p>
<p>The training point matters most for expectations. NICL said it has no obligation to offer regular employment during or after the apprenticeship, the contract ends after 12 months, and apprentices cannot claim permanent absorption on the basis of completing the programme. Training takes place at the allotted NICL office within the selected state, and an apprenticeship contract in NATS is mandatory. Applicants who need a permanent post should read this drive as a paid training year in a public-sector insurer, not as a route into a permanent NICL job.</p>
<h2>How selection works for NICL apprentices</h2>
<p>Selection is based on the percentage of marks obtained in the qualifying graduation examination, calculated up to two decimal places, followed by physical document verification. Shortlisted candidates receive instructions through their registered email address, and then appear in person at the designated NICL office with original certificates and self-attested copies. CGPA, OGPA, or GPA scores must be converted using the university's official formula. If two or more candidates obtain the same graduation percentage, the older candidate receives preference in the merit list.</p>
<p>No written examination or interview is mentioned in the notification, and the shortlisting date, document verification date, and apprenticeship commencement date have not been announced. Document verification arrangements will be communicated by registered email, so applicants must keep their email accounts active throughout the engagement process. Final engagement depends on eligibility verification, seat availability, and NATS contract approval.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the NICL Graduate Apprentice seats</h2>
<p>Applications are online only through the NATS portal. Applicants should register and complete their NATS student profile to 100 percent, then apply specifically against the National Insurance Company Limited apprenticeship opportunity using establishment ID EWBPNC096867. Creating a NATS student account alone is not sufficient. The notification does not specify an application or examination fee, so applicants should complete the application through the official NATS portal and follow only the instructions displayed there.</p>
<p>Applicants should apply only through the NATS portal and should not make payments to unverified recruitment agents or intermediaries. NICL does not charge through agents for this engagement, and any message offering a guaranteed seat for payment should be treated as a fraud attempt. Apply well before 18 November 2026 so a profile problem can still be fixed.</p>
<p>Other apprentice and bank coverage may help applicants compare options. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/indian-bank-apprentice-1500-posts-20261104">Indian Bank apprentice recruitment for 1,500 posts</a> is a larger training engagement, while <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/hcl-malanjkhand-trade-apprentice-171-posts-20261104">HCL trade apprentice recruitment at Malanjkhand</a> offers 171 trade seats. Readers may also want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/bob-wms-837-posts-20261104">Bank of Baroda WMS recruitment for 837 posts</a>, a fixed-term recruitment for experienced professionals rather than a fresher apprenticeship.</p>
<p><small>Sources: National Insurance Company Limited notification dated 4 November 2026 for engagement of 200 Graduate Apprentices under NATS for 2026-27, as summarised by FreeJobAlert at https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/nicl-graduate-apprentices-recruitment-2026-3078567 and corroborated by Karmasandhan at https://www.karmasandhan.com/nicl-apprentice-recruitment/; applications through the NATS portal at https://nats.education.gov.in. The notification states the seats, window, stipend, exclusions, and selection method quoted here; an application fee is not specified in the notification.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/nicl-graduate-apprentices-recruitment-2026-3078567','https://www.karmasandhan.com/nicl-apprentice-recruitment/','https://nats.education.gov.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO "Article" ("id", "slug", "category", "country", "titleEn", "titleNe", "excerptEn", "excerptNe", "bodyEn", "bodyNe", "sources", "publishedAt", "createdAt", "updatedAt") VALUES
(gen_random_uuid(), 'dhfws-purba-medinipur-67-posts-20261104', 'global', 'India',
'DHFWS Purba Medinipur Recruitment 2026: 67 NHM Contract Posts, Apply by 26 November',
'',
'District Health and Family Welfare Samiti, Purba Medinipur, has opened 67 contractual health posts, with online applications from 4 November 2026 to midnight of 26 November 2026.',
'',
$$<p>DHFWS Purba Medinipur recruitment 2026 opened on 4 November 2026, with the District Health and Family Welfare Samiti, Purba Medinipur, offering 67 contractual posts under the National Health Mission and National Urban Health Mission in West Bengal. The Samiti said online applications run from 4 November 2026 to midnight of 26 November 2026, with registration and fee payment closing on 25 November 2026, under Recruitment Notice-I, Memo No. CMOH/Pbmd/DPMU/6687, dated 2 November 2026.</p>
<p>Read the residence and contract limits before anything else, because they decide eligibility for every post in this drive. All applicants must be permanent residents of West Bengal and must know the local languages, and every essential qualification must be completed on or before the first date of online application. Community Health Assistant (Urban) posts are open only to female candidates who are permanent residents of Purba Medinipur and proficient in Bengali. All 67 posts are purely contractual to 31 March 2027, with extension depending on performance and government approval.</p>
<table><tr><th>At a glance</th><th>Details</th></tr><tr><td>Organisation</td><td>District Health and Family Welfare Samiti, Purba Medinipur</td></tr><tr><td>Department</td><td>Department of Health and Family Welfare, Government of West Bengal, under NHM/NUHM</td></tr><tr><td>Notice</td><td>Recruitment Notice-I, Memo No. CMOH/Pbmd/DPMU/6687, dated 2 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Total posts</td><td>67, across 10 posts</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly remuneration</td><td>Rs. 13,000 to Rs. 35,000, varying by post</td></tr><tr><td>Contract term</td><td>Purely contractual, initial period up to 31 March 2027</td></tr><tr><td>Application window</td><td>4 November 2026 to midnight of 26 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Registration and fee deadline</td><td>25 November 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Application fee</td><td>Rs. 100 for general categories, Rs. 50 for reserve categories, online only, non-refundable</td></tr><tr><td>Application mode</td><td>Online only, through the department website</td></tr><tr><td>Age limit</td><td>Counted as on 1 January 2026, varying by post, generally up to 40 years</td></tr></table>
<h2>DHFWS Purba Medinipur recruitment 2026: post-wise vacancies</h2>
<p>Pharmacist carries the largest share, with 17 posts, followed by Community Health Assistant (Urban) and Multi Rehabilitation Worker, with 12 posts each. Medical Officer-AYUSH (Mobile Health Team) has 6 male and 6 female posts, Staff Nurse has 6, Block Data Manager has 4, Public Health Manager has 2, and Senior Tuberculosis Laboratory Supervisor and Senior Treatment Supervisor have 1 post each. Those figures add up to the advertised total of 67.</p>
<p>Pay follows the post, not a single scale. Public Health Manager receives Rs. 35,000 a month, Medical Officer-AYUSH (male and female) receives Rs. 32,000, Staff Nurse, Senior Tuberculosis Laboratory Supervisor, and Senior Treatment Supervisor receive Rs. 25,000, Pharmacist and Block Data Manager receive Rs. 22,000, Multi Rehabilitation Worker receives Rs. 18,000, and Community Health Assistant (Urban) receives Rs. 13,000. No allowances on top of the monthly figure are mentioned.</p>
<h2>Who can apply for the Purba Medinipur health posts</h2>
<p>Qualifications differ sharply by post. Medical Officer-AYUSH posts need a BHMS, BAMS, or BUMS degree from a council-recognised institution, with internship completed at application and a council registration certificate. Pharmacist needs a two-year Diploma in Pharmacy (allopathic) from a Pharmacy Council of India or AICTE-approved institute, with a West Bengal Pharmacy Council registration certificate. Staff Nurse needs a General Nursing and Midwifery course from an Indian Nursing Council-recognised institute and West Bengal Nursing Council registration.</p>
<p>Public Health Manager accepts one of four alternative qualification routes: graduation in dental or nursing, a master's degree in a listed life science or economics subject, graduation in social science with a master's in public health or a related field, or graduation in any discipline with an MBA in human resources or health care. Computer efficiency, including MS Office and the internet, and two years of post-qualification experience in health programme management are also required. Block Data Manager needs graduation plus at least a one-year diploma in computer application from a government-registered institution, with three years in the government sector or five years in the private sector in data recording and analysis. Multi Rehabilitation Worker needs a physiotherapy bachelor's degree and two years of hospital experience, while the supervisor posts need graduation with a laboratory technology or science qualification, plus a permanent two-wheeler licence.</p>
<p>Age limits are counted as on 1 January 2026 and vary by post. Most posts carry a maximum of 40 years, with age relaxation as per government norms; the two supervisor posts carry a minimum of 21 years and a maximum of 40 years. The notice does not mention age relaxation for the two supervisor posts.</p>
<h2>How selection works for the Purba Medinipur posts</h2>
<p>Candidates are ranked under each post's scale of scoring, with academic marks in proportion to the percentage obtained. Medical Officer-AYUSH and Pharmacist posts each carry 100 marks across class 10, class 12, the qualifying degree or diploma, and additional marks for higher qualifications in the field. Public Health Manager posts carry 100 marks, including a 15-mark computer test and 10 marks for experience. Block Data Manager posts carry 100 marks, of which the computer component is worth 70.</p>
<p>Staff Nurse and Community Health Assistant (Urban) posts are scored on academic marks alone, at 100 marks each. Multi Rehabilitation Worker posts carry 50 marks across academics, experience, and interview, while the two supervisor posts carry 50 marks across academics, experience, and a computer test. Proportionate marking runs to two decimal points, original testimonials are verified, and candidates must go through every stage: the notice says a candidate who skips any stage will be disqualified immediately. Interview and shortlisting details will be published on wbhealth.gov.in and purbamedinipur.gov.in; no interview date has been announced yet.</p>
<h2>How to apply for the Purba Medinipur NHM posts</h2>
<p>Applications are online only, in the prescribed format on the department's website. Fill in the application, upload a signature and photograph, pay the fee online by 25 November 2026, and complete submission by midnight of 26 November 2026. The fee is Rs. 100 for general categories and Rs. 50 for reserve categories, deposited through online mode only, and is non-refundable. Download the print copy of the registration form from hr.wbhealth.gov.in and keep the registration number, since the employer says it is not liable to give that information later.</p>
<p>Applicants should apply only through the department's website and pay only through its official online route. Any message offering a guaranteed post in this recruitment for payment should be treated as a fraud attempt, and applicants should read the official notification for the full eligibility of their post before paying the fee. Experience counts only from the date the essential qualification was obtained, and certificates must come from the appointing authority.</p>
<p>Other government recruitment may help applicants compare options. <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/hprca-teacher-2423-posts-20261104">HPRCA teacher recruitment for 2,423 posts</a> takes applications from 10 November 2026 to 5 December 2026, while <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/gsssb-cce-1237-posts-20261104">GSSSB CCE recruitment for 1,237 posts</a> covers Class-3 posts in Gujarat. Readers may also want <a href="https://growentix.cloud/articles/supreme-court-junior-court-attendant-130-posts-20261104">Supreme Court Junior Court Attendant recruitment for 130 posts</a>, with applications closing on 25 November 2026.</p>
<p><small>Sources: District Health and Family Welfare Samiti, Purba Medinipur, Recruitment Notice-I, Memo No. CMOH/Pbmd/DPMU/6687, dated 2 November 2026, as summarised by FreeJobAlert at https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/dhfws-purba-medinipur-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-67-pharmacist-staff-nurse-and-more-posts-3078407 and corroborated by 9curry at https://www.9curry.com/organizations/dhfws-purba-medinipur; applications through the Department of Health and Family Welfare website at https://www.wbhealth.gov.in. The notice states the posts, pay, dates, fee, and contract terms quoted here; interview dates have not been announced.</small></p>$$,
'',
ARRAY['https://www.freejobalert.com/articles/dhfws-purba-medinipur-recruitment-2026-apply-online-for-67-pharmacist-staff-nurse-and-more-posts-3078407','https://www.9curry.com/organizations/dhfws-purba-medinipur','https://www.wbhealth.gov.in'],
NOW(), NOW(), NOW())
ON CONFLICT ("slug") DO NOTHING;
